  identity: "disjoint_chains_admitted_while_meeting_chains_decline" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a judgment declines the WEAKER incompatibility and admits the STRONGER one, because only the weak case has an arm** (a relation is built to decide pairs that are RELATED -- one nests inside the other, or the two meet on a shared link -- and every such pair gets a located, typed answer. Pairs that are wholly UNRELATED match no arm at all, fall through the whole procedure, and are admitted. The monotonicity a reader assumes is inverted: the further apart two things are, the more likely they are accepted. ",

    "WHY THIS IS ITS OWN CLASS AND NOT `absorbing_fallback`. The absorbing fallback WIDENS an answer to a superset while still answering the asked question. Here the question is never reached: no arm claims the pair, and the fallthrough is structural rather than a chosen degradation. It is also distinct from `lookup_miss_read_as_positive_classification`, where a miss MINTS a positive claim -- here nothing is minted, the value simply arrives at the end of the procedure unrefused, which is why it is invisible to any reviewer reading the arms rather than the exits. ",

    "SPECIMEN, at the DESIGN 4b floor (`values inhabit declared types`). A branded where-refinement value -- `HostIdentity`, declared `NonEmptyStr where brand(...)` -- passed at a formal declared as an ordinary product `Box` reaches no refusal at the direct call argument seam. The two refinement chains share no link. A pair whose chains MEET without nesting is reported undecidable and is therefore countable; this pair, whose chains are disjoint, is accepted. ",

    "ATTRIBUTION IS MEASURED ON BOTH SIDES AND THE DEFECT IS PRE-EXISTING. The discriminating control was authored while investigating review 62172, which attributed the hole to a where-refinement exclusion in the nominal-product arm. THAT ATTRIBUTION DOES NOT SURVIVE MEASUREMENT: the same control over the same fixtures and the same corpus, run against two compilers differing only in the three stage0 infer mirrors, evaluates false under BOTH. Removing the exclusion does not change the result, because the product arm was not making the refusal the exclusion was thought to suppress. The finding's CONCLUSION was right and its CAUSE was not, which is the reason this row records the mechanism rather than the review's account of it. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder -- silent wrongness, since a value of an unrelated constructor is ACCEPTED at a declared position with no diagnostic in either direction. CEILING: 3 (structurally guaranteed). Both sides' identities are decidable here -- each resolves to a declaration and each carries a refinement chain -- so a procedure that reaches a total decision over the pair can refuse this case from modeled structure rather than validating it afterwards. What stands between the class and its ceiling is not decidability but the absence of a total exit: the procedure has arms for the related cases and no arm for the unrelated one. ",

    "THE TELL THAT MAKES IT RECOGNISABLE ELSEWHERE, and it is a review instruction rather than a code smell: read the procedure's EXITS, not its arms. A decision procedure whose fallthrough is admission will look complete to anyone auditing the cases it handles, because every handled case is handled correctly. Ask instead what happens to an input no arm claims, and whether that answer is a decision or a default. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, at CAPABILITY grain: the declared-type inhabitance judgment REFUSES a produced value whose refinement chain is disjoint from the declared position's. Neither a control existing nor a diagnostic variant being declared retires this row -- both would be satisfied while the capability stays dead. The discriminating RED is enrolled and EXECUTING as `test.claim.declared_type_inhabitance_direct_call_witness.w_a_branded_refinement_at_an_unrelated_product_formal_still_refuses`, admitted `ExpectAssertionFalse`, and per DESIGN 4b(4) it does not retire when the wall lands: it flips to a permanent regression control.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
